      "content": "that's a good start for the overview. to make my detection algorithm more granular, i need to get into the specific \"logic\" they use to rationalize these views. for example, when they talk about \"racial preservation\" or \"threats,\" what are the specific pseudo-scientific or historical arguments they frequently cite to make those claims sound legitimate within their own community? i'm looking for the actual rhetoric they use to Frame their arguments, rather than just a summary of what they believe.",
